  i This Tailwind CSS value reads a CSS variable with [var()] instead of the shorthand.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
    2 │ <template>
  > 3 │ <div class="bg-[var(--brand)]"></div>
      │                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    4 │ <div :class="['w-[var(--width)]', { 'text-[var(--ink)]': active }]"></div>
    5 │ </template>
  
  i Tailwind CSS adds var() to a variable written in parentheses, so the shorthand is shorter and generates the same CSS.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Safe fix: Use the CSS variable shorthand.
  
    3 │ <div·class="bg-[var(--brand)]"></div>
      │                ----         -        

